---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---

<Base
  title="Disclaimer & Privacy"
  description="What coaching is and is not, and how your information is handled on this website."
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Please read" heading="Disclaimer & Privacy" />

  <section class="container-prose py-14 sm:py-20">
    <div class="prose prose-brand prose-lg max-w-none">
      <h2>Coaching is not therapy or medical care</h2>
      <p>
        Julienne Blackburn is a trauma-informed life coach. She is not a licensed therapist,
        psychologist, psychiatrist, counselor, physician, or attorney, and nothing offered through
        this website is therapy, medical treatment, a diagnosis, or legal advice.
      </p>
      <p>
        Coaching is forward-looking work: clarifying what is happening, setting boundaries, and
        making decisions about what comes next. It does not treat mental health conditions. If you
        are living with a condition that needs clinical care, please work with a licensed
        professional — and know that many people see a therapist and work with a coach at the same
        time, to good effect.
      </p>

      <h2>Descriptions of personality disorders</h2>
      <p>
        This site describes patterns of behavior associated with narcissistic, borderline,
        antisocial, and other Cluster B personality disorders in order to help people recognize
        emotional abuse. Nothing here diagnoses any individual. Only a qualified clinician can
        diagnose a personality disorder, and doing so requires evaluating that person directly.
      </p>

      <h2>Ministry, prayer, and deliverance</h2>
      <p>
        Prayer, deliverance ministry, and spiritual support are offered as ministry, not as
        healthcare, and are never a substitute for medical or mental health treatment. They are
        always optional. Declining them changes nothing about the coaching you receive.
      </p>

      <h2>If you are in crisis</h2>
      <p>
        This website is not monitored around the clock and is not a crisis service. If you are in
        immediate danger, call 911.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>National Domestic Violence Hotline:</strong> 1-800-799-7233, or text START to
          88788. Free, confidential, 24/7.
        </li>
        <li><strong>988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline:</strong> call or text 988.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your privacy</h2>
      <p>
        When you fill out a form on this site — the contact form, an art submission, or a testimony
        — the information you enter is sent to Julienne and stored by this website's hosting
        provider so she can read and reply to it. It is not sold, rented, or shared with anyone
        else.
      </p>
      <p>
        Art submissions and testimonies are only published after you have given explicit permission,
        with the credit you chose. You can ask for anything of yours to be removed at any time and
        it will be taken down.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some pages embed content from other services — a scheduling calendar, a video player. Those
        services may set their own cookies when you interact with them, under their own privacy
        policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Payment</h2>
      <p>
        Payments are made directly through Zelle, PayPal, or Venmo. This website never collects or
        stores card or bank details.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Anything here you would like explained, ask.
        {site.email ? (
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
        ) : (
          <a href="/contact">Use the contact page</a>
        )}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
